# DTF tier manifest: curation-rule-types  (#2947 / 1.7.0 foundation)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The typed-rule foundation is DB+API-side
# (curation_rules columns + dispatch seam), storage-independent.
#
# The feature (#2947): curation_rules grows `rule_type` (pattern |
# publisher_trust | popularity), `config` (JSONB engine params) and `scope`
# (repository | global). The rules CRUD accepts + returns the new fields,
# validates rule_type/config/scope, and `GET /rules?scope=global` lists the
# instance-wide baseline. The legacy pattern engine must be byte-for-byte
# unchanged.
#
# Oracle (discriminating):
#   (TYPED)     admin POST /api/v1/curation/rules with rule_type=
#               publisher_trust + config + scope=global -> 201 and the response
#               ECHOES rule_type/config/scope; GET /rules?scope=global contains
#               it. On a pre-#2947 image serde silently drops the unknown
#               fields, so the echo/list assertions are RED.
#   (VALIDATE)  rule_type=mystery -> 400 Validation. Pre-#2947: 201 (RED).
#   (REGRESSION) a staging-scoped legacy 3-field pattern rule (telnet* block)
#               still enforces: seeded pending curation_package telnet-server
#               -> POST /packages/re-evaluate(default allow) -> status=blocked.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives an admin login plus ~10
# back-to-back API calls; the base default (ON) would throttle them.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
